Stream-able
===========

Stream-able is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE). It is a derivative
work of **Record-able** by JoEusebe (Minewind's Jo Eusebe), used and
redistributed under the MIT License; the original copyright and permission
notice are preserved in LICENSE, as the MIT License requires.

Nothing in this project is copied from OBS Studio. OBS is referenced only as
inspiration for workflow and terminology ("browser source", "transform box",
"multistreaming").


What was inherited from Record-able
-----------------------------------
These files are ported from Record-able; each carries a header naming its
origin:

  dev/streamable/audio/AudioCapture.java            (device detection)
  dev/streamable/audio/JavaAudioCapture.java        (Java Sound capture)
  dev/streamable/audio/OpenALAudioCapture.java      (OpenAL capture)
  dev/streamable/audio/OpenALLoopbackCapture.java   (OpenAL loopback game audio)
  dev/streamable/audio/WASAPIAudioCapture.java      (Windows loopback helper)
  dev/streamable/ffmpeg/FfmpegBundleManager.java    (now a thin shim; downloads
                                                     moved to the verified
                                                     runtime manager)
  dev/streamable/ffmpeg/EncoderType.java
  dev/streamable/ffmpeg/MediaCodecEncoder.java
  dev/streamable/recording/VideoMetadata.java       (probing, thumbnails, duration)
  dev/streamable/recording/DiskSpaceGuardian.java
  dev/streamable/util/PlatformUtils.java            (platform detection)

dev/streamable/util/PerformanceMetrics.java keeps Record-able's public API but
was reimplemented without the Micrometer dependency.


