* Inter typeface (https://github.com/rsms/inter), Copyright 2016 The Inter
  Project Authors: SIL Open Font License 1.1. Licence text:
  licenses/Inter-OFL-1.1.txt


Downloaded on demand (never bundled)
------------------------------------
Stream-able's runtime manager downloads these only when needed (or when the
player presses Install), over HTTPS, pinned to an exact version and SHA-256 in
the bundled manifest (assets/streamable/runtime/manifest.json). Nothing is
executed before its checksum is verified.

* FFmpeg 8.1.3, GPL build by BtbN (https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds):
  GPL-3.0-or-later, including x264 and x265. Run as a separate program;
  Stream-able never links against it. Source: https://ffmpeg.org and the
  build scripts in the BtbN repository.
* Chromium browser engine: jcef-natives (JCEF + Chromium Embedded Framework,
  BSD-3-Clause; Chromium, BSD-3-Clause plus the third-party licences listed in
  the downloaded package). Installed into MCEF Modern's directory.
* ONNX Runtime 1.30.0 (https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime), Microsoft:
  MIT. Its third-party notices ship inside the downloaded artifact
  (ThirdPartyNotices.txt). Used only for local noise cancellation.
* Noise-cancellation models, all run locally; no audio is ever uploaded:
    - DPDFNet-2 48 kHz (https://github.com/Ceva-IP/DPDFNet), Ceva:
      Apache License 2.0 for code and weights.
    - DPDFNet "baseline" 16 kHz checkpoint (the DeepFilterNet2 architecture
      with zero DPRNN blocks, from the same Ceva repository): Apache
      License 2.0. Shown in the UI as "DeepFilterNet2 (16 kHz)".
    - GTCRN (https://github.com/Xiaobin-Rong/gtcrn), Xiaobin Rong: MIT,
      weights distributed in the MIT-licensed repository.

DeepFilterNet (https://github.com/Rikorose/DeepFilterNet, MIT or Apache-2.0)
was studied for its streaming design; no code or weights from that repository
are included or downloaded.


Optional integration
--------------------
Plasmo Voice is supported through its public client API when the player has it
installed. It is not bundled or downloaded by Stream-able.
